    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d432">

                <pb facs="0445" n="347" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg347"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Choate to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1900-08-14"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August 14, 1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 383.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 381, of 11th
                    instant, I have the honor to inclose herewith the copy of a telegram<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d432-f1"/> which I received from you on the 12th instant, and
                    which I lost no time in communicating to Her Majesty’s Government.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph H. Choate.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d432-f1" n="2" xml:id="d432-f1-content">
                <p>Circular telegram printed ante, <ref target="#pg301">p. 301</ref>.</p>
